Feature client layer
---------------------------
May receive terminal connection errors, but never identity terminal or retryable connection errors

Will receive retryable pub/sub/unsub errors and the feature client must decide how to respond.

Should safely assume necessary subscriptions at all times that a connection is present


ConnectionClient layer
---------------------------


re-sends pub/sub/unsubs from feature clients as connection is available
Handles identity terminal exceptions internally (re-provision as necessary)


failure cases to consider:
  identity terminal exception encountered while device is otherwise idle.
    - Expect device to reprovision + redo birth flow for the user and halt all outgoing feature client traffic in the meantime
  


This layer is getting complicated enough that I want to factor out a lot of stuff that it shares with both gen2 and unified. Pain in the butt to do that with the birth flow? Maybe we need a higher level layer that just responds to identity-terminal errors by handling re-provisioning? Calling ProvisionAndConnect already abstracts all the birth flow specifics per gen.



MqttConnectionManager layer
---------------------------

Handles all retryable connection errors internally
Reports any terminal or identity terminal exceptions

bubbles up all pub/sub/unsub errors immediately





